## Verification

- `npm run build`: passed with Vite 7.3.7, 54 modules transformed, 4.25 s. An independent Vite build of `src/water/ocean.js` also passed: 36,249-byte ES module with Three external.
- Verified the 512² shore texture, exact new bounds, R-float 4096×1 coast texture, format/type and range. All 4096 LUT entries equal `Math.fround(field.coastX(z))` at their generated z samples.
- Confirmed the old sine coefficients are absent, ocean and surf share the same coast/shore/FFT texture objects, and every declared custom uniform has a binding.
- Re-ran independent direct DFT at nonzero time: relative error `6.3896e-8`, residual imaginary height `1.4426e-15`; deep-water dispersion checks passed.
- Checked seeded rebuild determinism for all ribbon timing and spray particle attributes, random length/lifetime/travel ranges, 24 Hz throttling, `engine.registry.surfPeriod`, and the backward-compatible test-camera structure.
- Checked actual curl/rise profile separation and overhang, gravity source, 56/40 instance counts, 112/80 spray counts, surf/total triangle budgets and renderOrder 1/2/3. All three materials retain premultiplied alpha, disabled depth writes and enabled depth tests. No reserved `patch`, `Math.random`, `Date.now` or 384 shore-data call was found in water source.

## Known gaps / integration

- No browser or server was started and no new screenshot was captured. Runtime GLSL compilation, actual curl readability, spray appearance, coast alignment, land/path masking and shallow-fish compositing still require the director's browser QA. Node geometry checks are not visual confirmation.
- Breakers are seeded periodic geometric events, not a fluid simulation or FFT wave-collision solve. Coast normal is a local LUT derivative; exposed rocks and animals do not alter the trajectory. The 512 height mask is approximate at sub-texel reef edges.
- Alpha remains a terrain-depth scalar approximation, without per-object scene-depth absorption or refractive UV distortion. Reflections remain analytic sky/sun. Water and surf do not cast/receive shadows.
- Outside the 512 shore bounds, depth still uses the simplified bed fallback while coastX follows the full LUT. Any future transparent object behind the surf needs compatible ordering; water and surf do not write depth.
- Main integration already calls `buildOcean`; no main, field, package or other module change is requested. Audio may read the provided `engine.registry.surfPeriod`.
